This suite runs the pynfs NFSv4.0, 4.1 and 4.2 server conformance tests
against the ganesha (FSAL_CEPH) export, one job per version. pynfs uses its
own NFS client, so there is no kernel mount here.

Delegations are enabled (cephadm's ganesha config disables them) so that the
DELEG tests exercise libcephfs delegations.

pynfs always exits 0. The pynfs task parses its JSON results and fails the
job on any failed test that is not listed under known_failures in
2-pynfs.yaml. The known failures, and why they fail:

  COMP3 LINK8 LOOK7 OPEN13 RM5 RNM8 RNM9 SEC6   (4.0; COMP3 RNM8 RNM9 on 4.1/4.2)
    Names that are not valid UTF-8 are expected to be rejected with
    NFS4ERR_INVAL. Ganesha does not validate UTF-8 by default.

  WRT16 WRT17   (4.0)
    pynfs bug: float division under python3 in st_write.py makes the tests
    error out before checking the server.

  PUTFH3   (4.0)
    A filehandle of a removed file is still usable (NFS4_OK, not
    NFS4ERR_STALE). The test notes that a server is allowed to do this.

  DELEG7   (4.1, 4.2)
    Ganesha ignores the callback security parameters set by BACKCHANNEL_CTL;
    CB_RECALL is sent with the credentials given at CREATE_SESSION.

  DELEG24 DELEG25   (4.1, 4.2)
    Ganesha does not support the FATTR4_OPEN_ARGUMENTS attribute, which the
    CB_GETATTR tests require.

  ALLOC1 ALLOC2 ALLOC3   (4.2)
    ALLOCATE returns NFS4ERR_NOTSUPP: libcephfs fallocate() does not support
    mode 0 (plain preallocation).

When a ganesha, libcephfs or pynfs fix lands, drop the test from
known_failures. The task logs any known failure that did not fail.
